{* =========================================================================
   aLatteX Demo 5 - document fields, template variables, and $evo

   aLatteX hands Latte the whole document array three times over:

     $pagetitle, $alxTags, ...   every field and TV, spread as bare variables
     $documentObject             the same thing as an array
     $evo                        the Evolution CMS core object itself

   A template variable is just another key in that array, so a TV attached to
   this template is readable as {$alxSubtitle} with no ceremony - and, unlike
   [*alxSubtitle*], it is readable *as a value*: sliced, counted, compared,
   passed to a filter.
   ========================================================================= *}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="{evoSetting('manager_language') ?: 'en'}">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <title>{$pagetitle} - aLatteX demo</title>
</head>
<body class="alx alx-tvs">

{{aLatteXDemoHeader}}

<section id="fields">
    <h3>Document fields</h3>
    <table>
        <tr><th>id</th><td>{$id}</td></tr>
        <tr><th>pagetitle</th><td>{$pagetitle}</td></tr>
        <tr><th>longtitle</th><td>{$longtitle ?: '(empty)'}</td></tr>
        <tr><th>alias</th><td>{$alias}</td></tr>
        <tr><th>published</th><td>{$published ? 'yes' : 'no'}</td></tr>
        <tr><th>menutitle</th><td>{$menutitle ?: $pagetitle}</td></tr>
    </table>

    <p>
        The same fields the EVO way, for comparison:
        [*id*] / [*pagetitle*] / [*alias*]
    </p>
</section>

<section id="tvs">
    <h3>Template variables</h3>

    <h4>alxSubtitle - a plain text TV</h4>
    <ul>
        <li>As a Latte variable: {$alxSubtitle}</li>
        <li>Through the helper: {evoTv('alxSubtitle')}</li>
        <li>As an EVO tag, resolved after Latte: [*alxSubtitle*]</li>
        <li>Filtered, which only the first two forms allow: {$alxSubtitle|upper|truncate:24}</li>
    </ul>

    <h4>alxTags - a multi-value TV</h4>
    {* Evolution CMS stores checkbox and multi-select values joined with ||.
       Latte turns that back into an array, which is the whole reason to reach
       for a template language here. *}
    {var $tags = ($alxTags|explode:'||')}
    <p>Raw value: <code>{$alxTags}</code></p>
    <p>{count($tags)} tags:</p>
    <ul class="alx-tags">
        <li n:foreach="$tags as $tag" n:class="alx-tag, $tag === 'latte' ? alx-tag--primary">
            {$tag|firstUpper}
        </li>
    </ul>
    <p n:if="in_array('latte', $tags, true)">This document is tagged "latte".</p>

    <h4>alxImage - an image TV</h4>
    {* Guard it: an image TV is empty until someone picks a file. *}
    {if $alxImage}
        <img src="{evoSetting('site_url')}{$alxImage}" alt="{$pagetitle}">
    {else}
        <p class="alx-empty">No image chosen for this document.</p>
    {/if}

    <h4>A TV that is not attached to this template</h4>
    <p>
        Absent keys are simply missing from the array, so read them
        defensively: {$alxNotAttached ?? 'not attached to this template'}
    </p>
</section>

<section id="documentobject">
    <h3>$documentObject</h3>
    <p>Everything above, as one array. Useful for loops and for debugging:</p>
    <ul>
        {foreach ['id', 'alias', 'template', 'alxSubtitle', 'alxTags'] as $key}
            <li><code>{$key}</code>: {$documentObject[$key] ?? '(absent)'}</li>
        {/foreach}
    </ul>
    <p>The document has {count($documentObject)} keys in total.</p>
</section>

<section id="core">
    <h3>$evo</h3>
    <p>
        The core object is in scope, so anything the CMS can answer during
        OnLoadWebDocument is available to the template.
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li>Site name: {$evo->getConfig('site_name')}</li>
        <li>Active parser: {$evo->getConfig('chunk_processor')}</li>
        <li>Manager language: {$evo->getConfig('manager_language')}</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        Prefer the helpers - {l}evoSetting('site_name'){r} and friends - where
        one exists. They read the same values and keep the template working if
        the core API moves.
    </p>
</section>

<main class="alx-content">[*content*]</main>

{{aLatteXDemoFooter}}

</body>
</html>
